<section class="products section container" id="products"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">Our equipment</span><h2>Featured Products</h2></div><a class="text-link" href="/products/static-eliminator">Explore product range <span>→</span></a></div><div class="product-grid">
<article class="product-card"><a class="product-image bar-image" href="/products/static-eliminator/st-g-series"><span class="product-tag">Pulsed AC</span><img src="/assets/home/core-bars.webp" alt="ST-G intelligent ionizing bar" width="1130" height="213" loading="lazy"></a><div class="product-copy"><h3>Ionizing Bars</h3><p>ST-G pulsed AC bars with integrated high-voltage generation and a 24 V DC input.</p><a href="/products/static-eliminator/st-g-series">View Details <span>↗</span></a></div></article>
<article class="product-card"><a class="product-image" href="/products/static-eliminator/ionizing-air-blowers"><span class="product-tag">Workstation ionization</span><img src="/assets/home/blower.webp" alt="ST-S200 desktop ionizing air blower" width="1200" height="900" loading="lazy"></a><div class="product-copy"><h3>Ionizing Air Blowers</h3><p>Local ionization for component handling and assembly.</p><a href="/products/static-eliminator/ionizing-air-blowers">View Details <span>↗</span></a></div></article>
<article class="product-card"><a class="product-image" href="/products/cleaning-machine/contact-cleaning-machine"><span class="product-tag">Surface cleaning</span><img src="/assets/home/core-cleaning.webp" alt="Shidike contact cleaning machine" width="729" height="838" loading="lazy"></a><div class="product-copy"><h3>Cleaning Machines</h3><p>Dry-contact cleaning for film, sheets and sensitive surfaces.</p><a href="/products/cleaning-machine/contact-cleaning-machine">View Details <span>↗</span></a></div></article>
</div></section>

<section class="problems-section" id="problems"><div class="container section"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">Start with your challenge</span><h2>Common Static Control &amp; Web Cleaning Problems</h2></div><p>Find practical guidance on film dust removal, static charge, ESD and sheet handling, with links to relevant equipment and testing methods.</p></div><div class="problem-grid" role="region" aria-label="Production line problems" tabindex="0"><article class="problem-card"><button type="button" data-open-image="/assets/home/dust-returns.webp" data-image-caption="Dust particles returning to a charged material surface" aria-label="Enlarge Dust Returns After Cleaning image"><img src="/assets/home/dust-returns.webp" alt="Dust particles returning to a charged material surface" loading="lazy"></button><div><h3>Why Does Dust Return After Film Cleaning?</h3><p>Electrostatic attraction can pull airborne particles back onto film or sheets after web cleaning. Pair suitable ionization with particle removal and collection, then review downstream rollers and handling to identify where the surface may pick up charge or contamination again.</p><a href="/guides/what-is-web-cleaning">Web Cleaning &amp; Dust Removal <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article class="problem-card"><button type="button" data-open-image="/assets/home/film-jam.webp" data-image-caption="Plastic film sticking and wrinkling around production rollers" aria-label="Enlarge Film Sticks or Misfeeds image"><img src="/assets/home/film-jam.webp" alt="Plastic film sticking and wrinkling around production rollers" loading="lazy"></button><div><h3>Can Static Make Plastic Film Stick?</h3><p>Static charge can make film cling to rollers or cause sheets to stick together, disrupting feeding and alignment. Check charge alongside web tension and mechanical settings, then assess an ionizing bar at the unwind, separation point or infeed.</p><a href="/products/static-eliminator#bars">Anti Static Bars for Film Lines <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article class="problem-card"><button type="button" data-open-image="/assets/home/operator-shock.webp" data-image-caption="Operator receiving a static discharge from plastic film" aria-label="Enlarge Operators Feel Static Shocks image"><img src="/assets/home/operator-shock.webp" alt="Operator receiving a static discharge from plastic film" loading="lazy"></button><div><h3>Why Do Operators Get Static Shocks?</h3><p>Charge can build up on materials, people or isolated equipment and discharge when they touch. Review personnel and equipment grounding under your site procedures, then assess suitable ionization for insulating materials at the handling point.</p><a href="/guides/how-to-prevent-static">Static Shock Prevention Guide <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article class="problem-card"><button type="button" data-open-image="/assets/home/component-failure.webp" data-image-caption="Electronic components being assembled on a PCB production line" aria-label="Enlarge ESD During Assembly image"><img src="/assets/home/component-failure.webp" alt="Electronic components being assembled on a PCB production line" loading="lazy"></button><div><h3>How Can ESD Damage PCB Components?</h3><p>Electrostatic discharge (ESD) can damage sensitive PCB components during handling, placement or assembly, and some damage may not be immediately detected. Review grounding, packaging and material transfer, then assess ionization as part of the full ESD control process.</p><a href="/products/static-eliminator/ionizing-air-blowers">ESD Ionizers &amp; Air Blowers <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article class="problem-card"><button type="button" data-open-image="/assets/home/stack-misregister.webp" data-image-caption="Charged sheets forming a misaligned stack" aria-label="Enlarge Stacks Lose Alignment image"><img src="/assets/home/stack-misregister.webp" alt="Charged sheets forming a misaligned stack" loading="lazy"></button><div><h3>Can Static Disrupt Sheet Stacking?</h3><p>Static attraction and repulsion can affect how sheets separate and settle, contributing to uneven piles or double-feeding. Review guides and feed settings alongside charge measurements, then assess ionization where sheets leave the conveyor or enter the stacker.</p><a href="/products/static-eliminator#bars">Ionizing Bars for Sheet Handling <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article><article class="problem-card"><button type="button" data-open-image="/assets/home/surface-voltage-measurement.webp" data-image-caption="Surface voltage meter measuring static charge on moving film" aria-label="Enlarge Uncertain Treatment Results image"><img src="/assets/home/surface-voltage-measurement.webp" alt="Surface voltage meter measuring static charge on moving film" loading="lazy"></button><div><h3>How Do You Check Static Neutralization?</h3><p>Compare material surface voltage readings before and after treatment using the same instrument position and production conditions. Test ionizer decay time and ion balance separately, then check the actual cleanliness or handling result against the requirements of your process.</p><a href="/guides/what-is-an-ionizing-bar">How to Test an Ionizing Bar <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></article></div><p class="problem-scroll-hint">Swipe to explore all six issues <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></p></div></section>

<section class="section container applications-section" id="applications">
  <div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">Equipment in context</span><h2>Applications &amp; Production Processes</h2></div><p>Start with your material and see where static control and cleaning fit.</p></div>
  <div class="applications-row" role="region" aria-label="Production applications" tabindex="0">
    <article class="application-tile" aria-labelledby="application-tile-1">
      <button type="button" class="application-tile-image" data-open-image="/assets/home/roll-to-roll-line.webp" data-image-caption="Roll-to-roll film production" aria-label="Enlarge Roll-to-roll film production"><img src="/assets/home/roll-to-roll-line.webp" alt="Roll-to-roll film production" width="960" height="540" loading="lazy"><span>Roll-to-roll film production <b>↗</b></span></button>
      <div class="application-tile-copy">
        <div class="application-tile-heading"><span class="application-tile-index" aria-hidden="true">01</span><h3 id="application-tile-1">Film &amp; Converting</h3></div>
        <p>Assess static charge along film unwinding, roller contact and rewinding. Select ionizing bar length and placement around the material width, line speed and handling path.</p>
        <p class="application-tile-process">Unwind · Infeed · Rewind</p>
        <a class="application-tile-link" href="#contact">Discuss Your Application <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="application-tile" aria-labelledby="application-tile-2">
      <button type="button" class="application-tile-image" data-open-image="/assets/home/smt-electronics.webp" data-image-caption="Electronics and SMT assembly workstation" aria-label="Enlarge Electronics and SMT assembly workstation"><img src="/assets/home/smt-electronics.webp" alt="Electronics and SMT assembly workstation" width="960" height="540" loading="lazy"><span>Electronics and SMT assembly workstation <b>↗</b></span></button>
      <div class="application-tile-copy">
        <div class="application-tile-heading"><span class="application-tile-index" aria-hidden="true">02</span><h3 id="application-tile-2">Electronics &amp; SMT</h3></div>
        <p>Assess local ionization for component handling and assembly, alongside grounding and other ESD controls. Review bar or blower placement, working distance and operating conditions.</p>
        <p class="application-tile-process">Handling · Placement · Assembly</p>
        <a class="application-tile-link" href="#contact">Discuss Your Application <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="application-tile" aria-labelledby="application-tile-3">
      <button type="button" class="application-tile-image" data-open-image="/assets/home/pcb-fpc-ccl.webp" data-image-caption="PCB, FPC and display cleaning applications" aria-label="Enlarge PCB, FPC and display cleaning applications"><img src="/assets/home/pcb-fpc-ccl.webp" alt="PCB, FPC and display cleaning applications" width="960" height="540" loading="lazy"><span>PCB, FPC and display cleaning applications <b>↗</b></span></button>
      <div class="application-tile-copy">
        <div class="application-tile-heading"><span class="application-tile-index" aria-hidden="true">03</span><h3 id="application-tile-3">PCB, FPC &amp; Display</h3></div>
        <p>Review particle removal and static control for PCB, FPC and display materials. Confirm cleaning compatibility, material support and downstream handling before selecting the equipment.</p>
        <p class="application-tile-process">Cleaning · Transfer · Charge checks</p>
        <a class="application-tile-link" href="#contact">Discuss Your Application <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
  <p class="applications-row-hint">Swipe to explore all three applications <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></p>
</section>

<section class="services-section refined-services" id="services" aria-labelledby="refined-services-title">
  <div class="container section">
    <div class="section-heading refined-services-heading">
      <div><span class="eyebrow">Application support</span><h2 id="refined-services-title">From Your Process to the Right Setup</h2></div>
      <p>A practical conversation about the equipment, installation and checks your production line needs.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="refined-service-steps">
      <li>
        <div class="refined-step-top"><span class="refined-step-number">01</span><span class="refined-step-stage">Understand</span><span class="refined-step-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></div>
        <h3>Start with Your Material</h3>
        <p>Share the material, working width, line speed and the problem you see. Include existing charge measurements when available.</p>
        <span class="refined-step-detail">Material · Process · Observed problem</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div class="refined-step-top"><span class="refined-step-number">02</span><span class="refined-step-stage">Select</span><span class="refined-step-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></div>
        <h3>Choose &amp; Size the Equipment</h3>
        <p>Review a bar, blower or cleaning system for the task. ST-G lengths can be specified from 300 mm to 3 m, with dimensions confirmed in the drawing.</p>
        <span class="refined-step-detail">Product type · Length · Configuration</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div class="refined-step-top"><span class="refined-step-number">03</span><span class="refined-step-stage">Integrate</span><span class="refined-step-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></div>
        <h3>Plan the Installation</h3>
        <p>Discuss the mounting gap, available space, power connection and material path. Leave access for emitter cleaning and inspection.</p>
        <span class="refined-step-detail">Mounting · Connections · Access</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div class="refined-step-top"><span class="refined-step-number">04</span><span class="refined-step-stage">Maintain</span><span class="refined-step-arrow refined-step-end" aria-hidden="true">✓</span></div>
        <h3>Maintain &amp; Recheck</h3>
        <p>Confirm cleaning and inspection guidance for your model. Use the checks appropriate to your equipment, and compare material readings under consistent conditions.</p>
        <span class="refined-step-detail">Cleaning · Inspection · Measurement</span>
      </li>
    </ol>
    <div class="refined-services-contact"><p>Start with a description of your line and the issue you want to address.</p><a href="#contact">Discuss Your Application <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
  </div>
</section>


<section class="resources-section section container" id="resources"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">Practical reading for your production line</span><h2>Insights &amp; Guides</h2></div><a class="text-link" href="/guides">All guides <span>→</span></a></div><div class="resources-grid"><a class="resource-feature" href="/guides/what-is-an-ionizing-bar"><picture><source media="(max-width:800px)" srcset="/assets/home/hero-ionizing-bar-mobile.webp"><img src="/assets/home/hero-ionizing-bar.webp" alt="ST-G ionizing bar and ionization illustration" loading="lazy"></picture><div><span class="resource-tag">Static control basics</span><h3>What Is an Ionizing Bar?</h3><p>Understand ionization, working distance and the role of charge measurement.</p><span class="resource-link">Read Article →</span></div></a><div class="resource-list"><a href="/guides/how-to-prevent-static"><img src="/assets/home/core-bars.webp" alt="ST-G ionizing bar" loading="lazy"><div><span class="resource-tag">Static control</span><h3>How to Prevent Static in Industry</h3><p>Practical steps for grounding, ionization and checking static charge.</p><span class="resource-link">Read Article →</span></div></a><a href="/guides/what-is-web-cleaning"><img src="/assets/home/contact-cleaner.webp" alt="Contact cleaning machine" loading="lazy"><div><span class="resource-tag">Surface cleaning</span><h3>What Is Web Cleaning?</h3><p>Start with the substrate, contamination and material path.</p><span class="resource-link">Read Article →</span></div></a></div></div></section>

